  "goodToKnow": "Spätzle are soft Swabian egg noodles, traditionally scraped from a board into boiling water or pressed through a Spätzlepresse. Schwäbische Spätzle have had EU protected geographical status since 2012. Kässpätzle, baked with cheese and fried onions, are popular in Swabia and the Allgäu. The name probably means little sparrows, with the Swabian diminutive -le. The word is usually plural."
